{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794360767709,"sessionID":"ses_e37d7c906ffexH7bihwr6ciXQY","part":{"id":"prt_1c83c74c30017Ge0ijdm7NB7Dr","messageID":"msg_1c83c4dd6001HpRpUVIh6vUOCD","sessionID":"ses_e37d7c906ffexH7bihwr6ciXQY","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794360767709,"sessionID":"ses_e37d7c906ffexH7bihwr6ciXQY","part":{"id":"prt_1c83c74c6001yjBDFNp7aDcX2B","messageID":"msg_1c83c4dd6001HpRpUVIh6vUOCD","sessionID":"ses_e37d7c906ffexH7bihwr6ciXQY","type":"text","text":"Done. The app is complete and verified.\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`): SQLite in `./data/app.db` (users, tokens, conversions); `POST /api/auth/register` (201, returns token) and `/api/auth/login` (200, `{\"token\"}`) with hashed passwords and bearer tokens; `POST /api/base64/encode|decode` (nothing stored, 400 with `{\"error\"}` for invalid base64/UTF-8); `POST /api/conversions` (201, conversion + full `output`), `GET /api/conversions` (paged, newest first), `DELETE /api/conversions/{id}` (own rows only, 404 otherwise); Flask serves the Vite build with SPA fallback, `/api/*` never shadowed.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`, Tailwind v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`, only CSS is `src/index.css`): sign-in/register forms, username + Sign out, two text areas with Encode/Decode, Copy button, API error display, a \"Save to history\" switch (routes conversions through `POST /api/conversions` when on) and a history list with Delete buttons and paging.\n\n**One fix worth noting**: the scaffold's `requirements.lock` used `--hash` lines as a constraints file, which flips pip into `--require-hashes` mode and makes `pip install -r requirements.txt -c requirements.lock` fail in every pip version (I reproduced with 24.0 and 25.1.1). I stripped the hashes from the lock (pins kept, as the README sanctions) and added `werkzeug` to `requirements.txt` since the app imports it directly.\n\nVerified: `check_api.py` (workspace root, 50 end-to-end checks) passes; gunicorn run exactly like the Dockerfile CMD serves API + frontend with data surviving a restart; `npm ci` + `npm run build` reproduces cleanly; `tsc --strict` passes.","time":{"start":1794360767686,"end":1794360767689}}}
